# Memory Index — {{workspace_name}}

> Managed by gish. Every session loads this file in full, so every line here
> costs something in every session. Keep it an index: one trigger phrase and
> one link per line. The lesson itself lives in the linked note.
>
> **How to write a line** (see docs ch.19):
> - Write the trigger as the *symptom you will have* when the note matters,
>   not as the cause. "The tool said OK, so it is fixed" finds a note;
>   "tool reports are unreliable" does not.
> - If a failure can go both ways (missed alarm / false alarm, too loose /
>   too strict), name both directions, or one direction will never be found.
> - Before adding a line, run `gish index budget --workspace .`.

